## Requirements

- **R1** — `role`, `loopMaxConsecutive`/`loopCooldownMs`, `approvalTimeoutMs`,
  `workbenchVerbosity`, and the new `endGoal`, `model`, `thinking`, `effort`,
  `permissionPreset` are settable per-thread; an unset thread key inherits the
  room value; unset both → agent/hard default.
- **R2** — In a thread, bare `!config <key> <val>` writes the **thread** overlay;
  at top level (scope==room) it writes the **room** overlay (unchanged from today);
  `!config room <key> <val>` force-writes the **room** overlay from a thread.
- **R3** — `!config get` (in a thread) shows the resolved/merged view, labeling
  each value's source layer (`thread`/`room`/`default`). `!config reset <key>`
  clears the layer matching the resolved write target.
- **R4** — `model`, `thinking`, and `effort` are honored per-turn by the
  `claude-sdk` runtime (SDK `query` options). ACP runtimes self-manage these —
  documented as an honest limit, surfaced on set, never silently mis-applied.
- **R5** — `endGoal` is injected into each turn's prompt as an objective block,
  alongside the persona `role`.
- **R6** — A per-thread permission **`mode`** selects one of the four vetted
  presets (strict / ask-per-edit / auto / bypass). It may loosen `allow`/`ask` but
  the effective **`deny` is always `union(room deny, preset deny incl.
  DENY_FLOOR)`** — chat can never drop a terminal-set deny or the floor. Raw
  `allow`/`ask`/`deny`/`tiers`/`preset` stay terminal-only. Owner-gated, applied
  per-turn. (See Key Decisions for the full containment + residual risk.)
- **R7** — Context surface (owner-only, per-thread): `!context` lists active
  shared-context notes; `!context remove <n>` invalidates one; `!context add
  <text>` appends a free-form note. Reuses the knowledge fold and once-per-turn
  delivery.
- **R8** — No data migration: existing `cfg:channel/<roomId>` records stay valid
  as the inherited-default layer; no regression for room-set config in threads.
- **R9** — Prompt-injection invariant preserved for everything except the
  explicitly-chosen `mode` crossing: owner-only, pre-admit short-circuit; identity,
  allowlist, raw permissions, and `access.json` stay terminal-managed.

