## Key Technical Decisions

- **Project-then-merge, never concat deltas.** Room and scope are independent
  artifacts. Resolution projects **each** through the existing `projectChannelConfig`
  (already clamps per-field), then shallow-merges `{ ...roomCfg, ...scopeCfg }`.
  Scope key present wins; absent inherits room; absent both → omitted → consumer
  default. Concatenating raw deltas would let a room `_clear` wipe a scope key and
  mis-order across artifacts — rejected.

- **Scope==room collapses to today.** No thread → both layers read the same
  artifact → resolution short-circuits to `configFor(state, roomId)`.

- **Write target in the host, parser stays pure.** `parseConfigCommand` gains
  `target?: 'room' | 'scope'` (strips a leading `room` token, reports the requested
  target; never learns real ids). `handleCommand` computes `writeScope` and routes
  `configArtifact`, the admit `channel:`, **and** `latestConfigHash` to it (today
  all three hardcode `roomId` — the bug magnet).

- **model / thinking / effort are per-turn adapter options, not session state.**
  The SDK accepts them per `query()`. Extend the `AgentAdapter.prompt()` input with
  optional `{ model, thinking, effort }`; the Driver assembles them from the
  resolved per-thread config each turn; `claude-sdk` forwards them to `query`
  options; `acp` ignores them (honest limit). No session rebuild, no
  invalidation hook — changing any of them just takes effect next turn. (`runtime`,
  the only value that would need a session rebuild, is **deferred** — Scope.)

- **`thinking`/`effort` map to SDK types.** `thinking` enum → `ThinkingConfig`
  (`off`→`{type:'disabled'}`, `auto`→`{type:'adaptive'}`, `high`→`{type:'enabled',
  budgetTokens}`). `effort` enum → `EffortLevel` (`low|medium|high|xhigh|max`).
  Both `kind:'enum'` registry rows. `model` is `kind:'text'` (model ids churn; an
  enum would reject valid new ids) with non-empty single-token validation.

- **Permission `mode` containment (the boundary crossing).** Chat selects among
  the **4 vetted presets only** via a new `mode` chatKey → `permissionPreset` field;
  raw `allow`/`ask`/`deny`/`tiers`/`preset` stay in `TERMINAL_ONLY_KEYS`. At
  per-turn permission resolution: if the scope has `permissionPreset`, the base
  profile becomes `expandPreset(mode)` but with **`deny` overridden to
  `union(readRoomSettings.deny, expandPreset(mode).deny)`** — so a thread loosens
  `allow`/`ask` but never drops a terminal-set deny or the `DENY_FLOOR`. Per-actor
  `tiers` still apply on top (only tighten). The audit `classify-on-tool-request`
  injection is extended to resolve the same scope mode so the audit trail stays
  honest. **Residual risk accepted per decision:** the owner (only the owner — peers
  /humans can't reach `!config`) can set `bypass` per-thread; enforcement is correct
  via the per-turn adapter profile, and the floor + room deny always hold.

- **Context surface reuses existing machinery.** New `ContextControl` collaborator
  (modeled on `ChannelConfigControl`/`WatchControl`): `!context` renders
  `activeNotes(know:channel/<scopeId>/shared-context)`; `remove <n>` admits
  owner-role `knowledge.invalidate` (verb already exists); `add <text>` admits
  owner-role `knowledge.append` (same shape as session import). Once-per-turn
  delivery via the existing `pendingContext`/`pickFreshContext` path is unchanged.

