## Risks & Mitigations

- **`mode` crosses the prompt-injection boundary (highest).** Mitigated by:
  owner-only + pre-admit gate (peers/humans/injections can't reach `!config`);
  chat selects only among 4 vetted presets, never raw patterns; effective deny =
  union(room deny, floor) so a thread never drops a terminal-set protection;
  enforcement is the per-turn adapter profile (correct), and the audit injection is
  extended to match. Residual: the owner can set `bypass` per-thread — accepted per
  decision. Call out prominently in review + `docs/security-and-permissions.md`.
- **Mid-turn option change.** model/thinking/effort/mode all apply at turn *start*
  (resolved in `runTurnForChannel`); an in-flight turn is never mutated — change
  takes effect next turn. No session teardown.
- **`latestConfigHash`/`channel` following `roomId` not `writeScope`** (U3) — both
  hardcode `roomId` today; route both to `writeScope` or a thread set silently
  writes/chains the room artifact.
- **Audit fidelity** under a loosened thread (U6) — without the relay audit
  injection, `classify-on-tool-request` under-reports allows; U6 extends it.
- **UX change:** `!config role …` typed in a thread now writes the **thread**, not
  the room; document the `!config room …` modifier in help + confirmation.
- **`renderConfig` signature ripple** to all `channel-config.ts` callers; keep a
  room-only path for `get room`.
- **Context numbering races** — `remove <n>` maps to a hash via a stable sort
  (createdAt); re-list before remove. A concurrent append shifts numbers between
  list and remove (low-impact; owner-only).

