## Scope Boundaries

### Deferred to follow-up work
- **`runtime` as a per-thread knob** — the only value needing a session rebuild
  (selects which binary spawns; sandbox-downgrade hazard); stays terminal-only.
- **ACP `model`/`thinking`/`effort` pass-through** — ACP agents self-manage; needs
  protocol/client support.
- **Per-thread rate-cap / require-mention / mention-patterns** — gate inbound before
  a thread exists; not in target set.

### Out of scope (non-goals)
- Raw `allow`/`ask`/`deny`/`tiers`/`preset` authoring from chat — stays terminal
  only; only the named `mode` preset is chat-settable.
- Identity, allowlist, `access.json`, SDK `bypassPermissions`/
  `allowDangerouslySkipPermissions` — untouched (mode is achieved via knock-knock's
  own profile, not the SDK permission mode).
- Migrating existing fold records (none needed — R8).

